<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#prince-of-wales">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prince of Wales</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> was the title claimed by native Welsh rulers of Gwynedd as overlords of Wales. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-ap-gruffudd">Llywelyn ap Gruffudd</a> won English recognition of it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-montgomery">Treaty of Montgomery</a> in 1267, but was killed in 1282. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a> revived the title in 1400. Since 1301 it has been given by the English and then British crown to the heir to the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales.jpg" alt="Prince of Wales" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Personal_Banner_of_the_Prince_of_Wales.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
